§ `ss 370, 371 -- stealing (k021)`

-- k021: stopped at the door, but he had moved the goods, so the stealing was complete (s 371(6)); secrecy is not needed (s 371(3)).
#ASSERT `Did I steal it` `Jake's phone case and earbuds, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `Did I steal it` `the same goods, picked up but never moved`
#ASSERT NOT `Did I steal it` `a thing borrowed meaning to return it`
#ASSERT NOT `Did I steal it` `a found wallet kept, owner unknown and undiscoverable`
#ASSERT `Did I steal it` `a found wallet kept, owner's name inside`
#ASSERT NOT `Did I steal it` `a fixture never severed`
#ASSERT `Did I steal it` `goods taken under an honest claim of right`

-- s 22: an honest claim of right leaves the definition met but removes criminal responsibility.
#ASSERT `Can I be guilty of stealing it` `Jake's phone case and earbuds, 20 November 2021` (Date 30 8 2006) (Date 20 11 2021) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I be guilty of stealing it` `goods taken under an honest claim of right` (Date 30 8 2006) (Date 20 11 2021) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I be guilty of stealing it` `Jake's phone case and earbuds, 20 November 2021` (Date 1 1 2009) (Date 20 11 2021) FALSE

